  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows high volatility (spikes >5%) combined with neutral-to-positive sentiment; true outcomes often reverse direction within the first 3 days.",
    "When sentiment is positive (1.0) or mixed (0.25-0.33), the model overestimates the duration of price increases, failing to capture immediate mean reversion after a spike.",
    "Model forecasts are systematically lower than true outcomes during the initial 2-4 days of a volatility event, suggesting a lag in detecting sudden supply/demand shocks.",
    "In high-volatility regimes, the model's linear extrapolation ignores the 'mean-reverting' behavior typical of EU ETS auctions, where extreme highs or lows are followed by rapid stabilization.",
    "Sentiment history with a trailing positive value (e.g., 0.33) does not prevent the model from under-predicting immediate downside risk if recent price action shows consolidation."
  ]
}
